PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789164233
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A man has shot himself dead in Walsall
OL,6, after shooting and injuring three other
OL,7, people, say West Midlands police.
OL,9,FThe man shot three youths in the back
OL,10,Fand was threatening the occupants of a
OL,11,Fcar when a police van arrived. The
OL,12,Fthree teenagers suffered minor wounds.
OL,13,           F
OL,14,FAs police tried to persuade him to hand
OL,15,Fover the sawn-off shotgun, the man shot
OL,16,Fhimself dead.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FPolice say an "arsenal" of weapons was
OL,19,Ffound at the house of the dead man,
OL,20,FAnthony George Haskett, 18, of Walsall.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]CFrom 11-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789164233
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,V  -,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Foreign Secretary has announced
OL,6, Britain is to give an extra #1 million
OL,7, in aid to Sudan.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FSir Geoffrey, who is in Sudan at the
OL,10,Fstart of a tour of Africa, said the aid
OL,11,Fwas to help flood victims in the south.
OL,13,FRelief efforts are being hampered by
OL,14,Fa civil war in the region and Sir
OL,15,FGeoffrey called for reconciliation
OL,16,Fbetween the Sudanese government and
OL,17,Fthe rebels.
OL,19,FHe also promised a further #1 million
OL,20,Fto help fight plagues of locusts in
OL,21,Feast Africa.
OL,23,D]CFrom 11-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789164233
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Two members of the family of the former
OL,6, MP and broadcaster Mr Aiden Crawley
OL,7, were killed when their light aircraft
OL,8, crashed in Italy.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe Cesssna 210 was on a flight from
OL,11,FTurin to Luton, but crashed shortly
OL,12,Fafter take-off.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMr Andrew Crawley and his brother
OL,15,FRandall were killed in the crash.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FThe third person on board, a Turkish
OL,18,Fmechanic, was also killed.
OL,19,F
OL,20,FThe wreckage of the aircraft was found
OL,21,Fsome 30 miles from Turin.
OL,23,D]CFrom 11-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789164233
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A car bomb exploded in a busy street
OL,6, in the Afghan capital Kabul today
OL,7, killing 10 people and injuring 40.
OL,9,FThe Soviet news agency TASS said the
OL,10,Fvictims of the blast included women and
OL,11,Fchildren.
OL,13,FA car packed with explosives caused a
OL,14,Fgreat deal of damage to a commercial
OL,15,Fbuilding near the Pakistani embassy.
OL,16,F
OL,17,FAfghan guerrillas seeking the overthrow
OL,18,Fof the Soviet-backed Najibullah
OL,19,Fgovernment were blamed for the blast.
OL,20,F
OL,23,D]CFrom 11-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
