OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Pope John Paul II has celebrated the
OL,6, first mass of his southern African tour
OL,7, at the Borrowdale racecourse in the
OL,8, Zimbabwean capital, Harare.
OL,10,FThe Pope's call for reconciliation with
OL,11,FGod and with one another were directed
OL,12,Ftowards South Africa.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FChallenging the ideology of apartheid
OL,15,Fthe Pope said: "Father, you have given
OL,16,Fall peoples one common origin and your
OL,17,Fwill is to gather them as one family."
OL,19,FHe also referred to the suffering
OL,20,Fcaused by "sin such as racial
OL,21,Fdiscrimination and segregation".
OL,23,D]CFrom 11-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789164233
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/18
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Up to 50 million people all over the
OL,6, world are said to have taken part in
OL,7, this afternoon's global fun run being
OL,8, organised by Sport Aid.
OL,10,FAt least 120 countries joined the race
OL,11,Fwhich was televised to a potential
OL,12,Fworld audience of 1.5 billion.
OL,14,FThe main event in Britain was in
OL,15,FLondon's Hyde Park, where 100,000
OL,16,Fpeople ran the six-mile course.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe first Sport Aid Race Against Time
OL,19,Fwas in 1986; 20 million people ran and
OL,20,F#24 million was raised for charity.
OL,23,D]CFrom 11-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
